atre with a long table between vivid stage curtains"></figure><span class="stage-label">Westbourne Grove / London / Table open</span><div class="stage-marquee"><span>Guest count first · Objects second · Sightlines open · Service unhurried · Guest count first · Objects second · Sightlines open · Service unhurried ·</span></div></section>
<section class="course-ticker" id="home-02"><header><div><p class="kicker">02 / The running order</p><h2>Five cues. One generous evening.</h2></div><p>Move through the night with a plan light enough to disappear once everyone sits down.</p></header><div class="course-line"><article tabindex="0"><b>18:30</b><div><small>Cue 01</small><h3>Doors & water</h3><p>Give coats, glasses and first conversation a clear place to land.</p></div></article><article tabindex="0"><b>19:05</b><div><small>Cue 02</small><h3>First plate</h3><p>Serve a small opening course with most of its work finished early.</p></div></article><article tabindex="0"><b>19:50</b><div><small>Cue 03</small><h3>Main table</h3><p>Bring shared dishes within reach and keep the centre low.</p></div></article><article tabindex="0"><b>20:40</b><div><small>Cue 04</small><h3>Clear & pause</h3><p>Reset the surface without breaking the conversation.</p></div></article><article tabindex="0"><b>21:10</b><div><small>Cue 05</small><h3>Last course</h3><p>Let dessert, fruit or tea close the meal without a hard ending.</p></div></article></div></section>
<section class="ingredient-columns" id="home-03"><div class="ingredient-intro"><p class="kicker">03 / Ingredient columns</p><h2>Compose the whole table, not isolated objects.</h2><p class="lede">Every setting balances three forms of work: what guests need, what the food needs, and what the room can quietly support.</p></div><div class="ingredient-board"><article class="ingredient-card"><b>01</b><div><h3>People</h3><ul><li>Guest count</li><li>Reach</li><li>Sightline</li><li>Dietary needs</li></ul></div></article><article class="ingredient-card"><b>02</b><div><h3>Menu</h3><ul><li>Temperature</li><li>Texture</li><li>Serving vessel</li><li>Course pace</li></ul></div></article><article class="ingredient-card"><b>03</b><div><h3>Room</h3><ul><li>Table width</li><li>Light level</li><li>Clearing route</li><li>Open space</li></ul></div></article></div></section>
<section class="light-console" id="home-04"><div class="console-copy"><p class="kicker">04 / Lighting console</p><h2>Build a pool of light, not a wall of candles.</h2><p class="lede">Set flame below the natural sightline, keep sleeves and foliage clear, and leave enough ambient light for food, edges and steps.</p><a class="action dark" href="journal-03.html">Read the light note</a></div><div class="console-panel" aria-label="Suggested dinner lighting balance"><header><span>Room channel</span><span>Safe / unscented / low</span></header><div class="fader"><label>Ambient</label><span class="track" style="--level:58%;--tone:var(--lilac)"><i></i></span><output>58</output></div><div class="fader"><label>Table</label><span class="track" style="--level:72%;--tone:var(--yellow)"><i></i></span><output>72</output></div><div class="fader"><label>Accent</label><span class="track" style="--level:24%;--tone:var(--coral)"><i></i></span><output>24</output></div><p class="console-status"><i></i>Sightline channel remains open</p></div></section>
<section class="plate-stack" id="home-05"><header><div><p class="kicker">05 / Plate stack</p><h2>Give each object one clear job.</h2></div><p class="lede">A useful piece earns its place through food, drink, comfort or service. Decoration works best after those jobs are covered.</p></header><div class="stack-stage"><article class="stack-card"><b>01</b><span class="plate-mark">FRAME</span><div><h3>The plate</h3><p>Match its usable field to the portion and the way the food needs to be cut or shared.</p></div></article><article class="stack-card"><b>02</b><span class="plate-mark">HOLD</span><div><h3>The glass</h3><p>Choose stability, capacity and a comfortable grip before multiplying shapes.</p></div></article><article class="stack-card"><b>03</b><span class="plate-mark">SOFTEN</span><div><h3>The linen</h3><p>Use weave and drape to quiet sound, ground colour and support practical wiping.</p></div></article></div></section>
<section class="host-cue" id="home-06"><div class="cue-visual"><img src="assets/images/core-studio.svg" alt="Vivid kitchen pass with preparation tickets for count, timing and light"><div class="cue-ticket">Tonight / six guests<br>Warm plates at 19:42<br>Clear surface at 20:35</div></div><div class="cue-copy"><p class="kicker">06 / Host cue</p><h2>Prepare the route, then stay at the table.</h2><p class="lede">A little backstage thinking reduces the interruptions that make hosting feel like a performance.</p><ol class="cue-list"><li>Finish cold elements early</li><li>Assign every serving tool</li><li>Keep one landing surface open</li><li>Decide where used dishes wait</li></ol><a class="action pale" href="table-studio.html">Enter the studio</a></div></section>
<section class="season-gallery" id="home-07"><header><div><p class="kicker">07 / Market colours</p><h2>Let the menu provide the accent.</h2></div><p>Build a quiet ground, repeat one material tone, then allow seasonal ingredients to bring the highest colour.</p></header><div class="season-strip"><article class="season-tile"><img src="assets/images/journal-10.svg" alt="Angular seasonal produce collage in vivid market colours"><div><small>Market / 10</small><h3>Season carries colour</h3></div></article><article class="season-tile"><img src="assets/images/journal-07.svg" alt="Three overlapping colour fields showing a restrained palette"><div><small>Palette / 07</small><h3>Three tones are enough</h3></div></article><article class="season-tile"><img src="assets/images/journal-02.svg" alt="Four graphic linen swatches showing weave weight and drape"><div><small>Material / 02</small><h3>Texture changes the room</h3></div></article><article class="season-tile"><img src="assets/images/journal-08.svg" alt="Low botanical lines kept beneath an open sightline"><div><small>Centre / 08</small><h3>Keep the view open</h3></div></article></div></section>
<section class="journal-billboard" id="home-08"><header><div><p class="kicker">08 / Field notes</p><h2>Twelve practical reads from table to reset.</h2></div><p class="lede">Original, realistic guidance for everyday suppers, shared plates, small rooms and the objects already in your cupboard.</p></header><div class="billboard-list"><a href="journal-01.html"><b>01</b><span>Scale the table for the guest count</span><small>Open note ↗</small></a><a href="journal-03.html"><b>03</b><span>Set candle height and safe light</span><small>Open note ↗</small></a><a href="journal-09.html"><b>09</b><span>Pace the menu across the evening</span><small>Open note ↗</small></a><a href="journal-12.html"><b>12</b><span>Clear, dry and store tableware</span><small>Open note ↗</small></a></div></section>
<section class="last-course" id="home-09"><div class="last-stamp">TEP</div><div class="last-copy"><p class="kicker">09 / Last course</p><h2>Set less.<br>Notice more.</h2><p class="lede">Start with people, choose what earns its place, and let the evening carry the rest.</p><a class="action pale" href="journal.html">Read all twelve notes</a></div></section></main><footer><div><h3>Explore</h3><a href="table-studio.html">Table Studio</a><a href="setting-index.html">Setting Index</a><a href="journal.html">Serving Journal</a></div><div><h3>Contact</h3><p class="one-line">3638 Westbourne Grove, London, UK, W2 5SH, GB</p><a class="one-line" href="tel:+12125559857">+1 2125559857</a><a class="one-line" href="mailto:hello@tableessencepoint.com">hello@tableessencepoint.com</a></div><div><h3>Policies</h3><a href="privacy.html">Privacy</a><a href="terms.html">Terms</a><a href="refund.html">Refund</a><a href="shipping.html">Shipping</a></div></footer><aside class="consent" aria-label="Analytics preferences"><p>Optional analytics helps us improve the serving journal. Advertising storage stays disabled.</p><button type="button" data-consent="accept">Allow analytics</button><button type="button" data-consent="decline">Decline</button></aside><script src="assets/app.js"></script></body></html>